# The test library. A test is a meta object: a name and a work that runs and reports whether it held. `case` builds one, `run` executes a list of them, prints each result, and returns a tally. Assertions return a boolean: `want` for equality, `deny` for inequality. Every other check is an ordinary operator call (`is-above`, `is-below`, `contains`) returned directly. Tests are ordinary Term, so the compiler handles them with no special case. See note/library/seed/test-dsl.md.

load @term/seed/code/console
  find log

# the meta object a test block constructs: a name and the work that returns whether it passed

form test
  link name, like text
  link work
    like task
      note async
      like boolean

form report
  link pass, like number
  link fail, like number

# build a test meta object: what a test block lowers to

task case
  take name, like text
  take work
    like task
      note async
      like boolean
  like test
  send back
    make test
      bind name, read name
      bind work, read work

# assertions: each returns whether it held, so a work ends with `send back, call want ...`. `want` checks equality, `deny` checks inequality. Ordered and contains checks use the ordinary operators directly: `want got, expect, call is-above ...` is just `send back, call is-above`.

task want
  head t
  take got, like t
  take expect, like t
  like boolean
  send back
    call is-equal
      read got
      read expect

# the negation of want: got and expect must differ

task deny
  head t
  take got, like t
  take expect, like t
  like boolean
  send back
    call is-equal
      call is-equal
        read got
        read expect
      false

# run a list of tests, print each name and result, return a pass/fail tally

task run
  note async
  take cases
    like list
      like test
  like report
  save pass, code 0
  save fail, code 0
  walk list, read cases
    hook next
      take item, name row
      call log
        read row/name
      save held
        call row/work
          wait true
      fork test
        hook test, read held
        hook hold
          call log
            text <  ok>
          save pass
            call add
              read pass
              code 1
        hook miss
          call log
            text <  FAIL>
          save fail
            call add
              read fail
              code 1
  send back
    make report
      bind pass, read pass
      bind fail, read fail
